  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Any enters abilities of the copied creature will trigger when Clone enters. Any \"as [this creature] enters\" or \"[this creature] enters with\" abilities of the chosen creature will also work.",
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clone copies exactly what was printed on the original creature and nothing else (unless that creature is copying something else or is a token; see below). It doesn't copy whether that creature is tapped or untapped, whether it has any counters on it or Auras and Equipment attached to it, or any non-copy effects that have changed its power, toughness, types, color, or so on.",
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clone's ability doesn't target the chosen creature.",
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Clone somehow enters at the same time as another creature, Clone can't become a copy of that creature. You may choose only a creature that's already on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the copied creature has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.",
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the copied creature is a token, Clone copies the original characteristics of that token as stated by the effect that created the token.",
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the copied creature is copying something else (for example, if the copied creature is an Evil Twin), then Clone enters as whatever that creature copied.",
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can choose not to copy anything. In that case, Clone enters as a 0/0 Shapeshifter creature, and is probably put into the graveyard immediately.",
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card in a graveyard has {X} in its mana cost, X is 0.",
      "oracle_id": "a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0",
      "published_at": "2025-09-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If any abilities trigger on the creature entering the battlefield, those abilities resolve after you lose life. If losing life results in you losing the game, those abilities won't resolve.",
      "oracle_id": "a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0",
      "published_at": "2025-09-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, the creature you control from Reanimate is exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0",
      "published_at": "2025-09-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The amount of life you lose is determined by the mana value of the card in your graveyard, not the creature once it's on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0",
      "published_at": "2025-09-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You lose life after the creature is already on the battlefield. Any abilities it has that interact with loss of life, such as that of Platinum Emperion, apply to that loss of life.",
      "oracle_id": "a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0",
      "published_at": "2025-09-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the target card is no longer in the graveyard when Cremate tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't draw a card.",
      "oracle_id": "c6a2e410-b182-48d1-aeb2-bc8de27e9cd2",
      "published_at": "2012-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must be able to target a card in a graveyard to cast Cremate.",
      "oracle_id": "c6a2e410-b182-48d1-aeb2-bc8de27e9cd2",
      "published_at": "2012-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type (such as by Sea's Claim), it continues to be a creature and a Dryad.",
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2011-09-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.",
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2013-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Dryad Arbor is played as a land. It doesn't use the stack, it's not a spell, it can't be responded to, it has no mana cost, and it counts as your land play for the turn.",
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Due to its color indicator (appearing to the left of its type line), Dryad Arbor is green. Color indicators apply in all zones, not just the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Forest is a land type and Dryad is a creature type.",
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type, it continues to be a green Dryad creature.",
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a Dryad Arbor gains flash, or you have the ability to play Dryad Arbor as though it had flash (due to Teferi, Mage of Zhalfir or Scout's Warning, for example), you can ignore the normal timing rules for when during your turn you can play a land, but not any other restrictions. You can't play Dryad Arbor during another player's turn, and you can't play Dryad Arbor if you don't have any land plays remaining.",
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this creature enters at the same time as one or more other creatures, its ability will trigger for each of those other creatures. ",
      "oracle_id": "f3fad295-1af2-4ecc-8546-b121ad6be27b",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": 1,
  "source": "Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"
}
